# Deny-by-default safety net — protects proprietary model code and every
# unrelated local file (diagnostics, xG spreadsheets, cached HTML, CSV
# exports, Word docs, etc.) from ever being committed, even by an
# ordinary "git add ." Only the specific public track-record files
# below are ever allowed through; everything else stays local-only
# regardless of what gets added.
*

# The actual public-facing site
!index.html
!chart.umd.min.js
!track_record_data.js
!track_record_data.json
!public_predictions_log.csv
!public_predictions_log.js
!recent_results.js

# Real infrastructure files GitHub Pages itself needs
!CNAME
!.gitignore
